 s in Cancer: Health Policy and Oncology: Understanding Care and Outcomes i
 n a Changing Delivery System
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261013T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261013T170000
DTSTAMP:20261010T174029Z
UID:stanford_campus-localist-52561867818592-52561896386565@local-events
DESCRIPTION:The Stanford Cancer Institute Breakthroughs in Cancer seminar 
 series provides a platform for eminent leaders in oncology to share their 
 insights with the Stanford community. Seminars highlight innovations acros
 s basic\, translational\, clinical\, and population cancer science. \n\nJo
 in the Stanford Cancer Institute on Tuesday\, October 13\, 4-5 p.m.\, at A
 lway M106\, Alway Building\, or via Zoom\, for a presentation by Nancy Kea
 ting\, MD\, MPH\, Professor of Health Care Policy at Harvard Medical Schoo
 l.\n\nDr.\n\nAges: All ages\nSource: https://stan.md/49eb9Wk\nLast synced:
  2026-10-10 10:40 PDT
LOCATION:E.D. Stone - Alway Building
URL:https://stan.md/49eb9Wk
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:[Stanford Humanities Center / Division of Literatures\, Cultures\,
  and Languages] Will and Attention: Meghan O’Gieblyn in conversation wit
 h Professor Laura Wittman
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261013T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261013T183000
DTSTAMP:20261010T174029Z
UID:stanford_campus-localist-54134630587523-54134630589572@local-events
DESCRIPTION:Meghan O'Gieblyn\, author of Interior States (2018) and God\, 
 Human\, Animal\, Machine (2021)\, will be in conversation with Professor L
 aura Wittman on Tuesday\, October 13th\, at Levinthal Hall in the Stanford
  Humanities Center. Meghan will discuss her new book\, Will and Attention 
 (2026): at once an undefended account of her relapse into alcoholism\, an 
 investigation of the concept of attention\, and an exquisitely written med
 itation on the limits of the self's ability to will its own change.\n\nThi
 s even\n\nAges: All ages\nSource: https://forms.cloud.microsoft/Pages/Resp
 onsePage.aspx?id=y3NlOXjzaEubyBV1XAxR86vnNC079xpArXyuBy2-gcNUMUNLMVhBRFJSV
 1lNVEFSSElEMEVDODhQWC4u\nLast synced: 2026-10-10 10:40 PDT
LOCATION:Humanities Center
URL:https://forms.cloud.microsoft/Pages/ResponsePage.aspx?id=y3NlOXjzaEuby
 BV1XAxR86vnNC079xpArXyuBy2-gcNUMUNLMVhBRFJSV1lNVEFSSElEMEVDODhQWC4u
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:[Abbasi Program in Islamic Studies / Feminist\, Gender\, and Sexua
 lity Studies] Why amina wadud Should Be as Famous as Malcolm X: The Life a
 nd Work of a Great American Feminist and Muslim Scholar-Activist | Carla P
 ower
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261013T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261013T190000
DTSTAMP:20261010T174029Z
UID:stanford_campus-localist-54137696929604-54137776565611@local-events
DESCRIPTION:Carla Power frames wadud not just as a leading Islamic scholar
  and activist\, but as an American public intellectual with a global impac
 t. Drawing on archival materials\, she will discuss wadud’s journey\, fr
 om her childhood as a Methodist preacher’s daughter from an economically
  disadvantaged background\, to her adolescence spent living with white fam
 ilies in Massachusetts\, through to her decades spearheading civil rights 
 movements on four continents–all while a single mother of five.\n\nCriti
 cal to\n\nAges: All ages\nLast synced: 2026-10-10 10:40 PDT
LOCATION:Encina Commons
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:[Explore Energy House / Precourt Institute for Energy] Advancing I
 ndigenous-led Pathways for Just and Vibrant Communities
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261013T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261013T192000
DTSTAMP:20261010T174029Z
UID:stanford_campus-localist-54169442429822-54169442430847@local-events
DESCRIPTION:Muwekma-Tah-Ruk and Explore Energy House invite members of the
  campus community for dinner and discussion with Native Roots Network\, wh
 ich is devoted to advancing Indigenous-led pathways for just and vibrant c
 ommunities.  \n\nLand restoration\, river restoration\, and language prese
 rvation are among their many pursuits\, including development of a Communi
 ty Resilience Center.  Plans for the Center include a Native Plants Garden
  and a renewable energy microgrid -- one similar to the new microgrid at t
 \n\nAges: All ages\nLast synced: 2026-10-10 10:40 PDT
LOCATION:Muwekma-Tah-Ruk
END:VEVENT
